title: Genres driving each other
intro: Every genre names what it does and what it knows, and takes the input only while it has it. So a card spawns an enemy, a hotspot opens a door, a note fires a weapon and a bumper hurts a boss, with no code.
project: Empty | Mix Kit

chapter: A card spawns an enemy | A Card Effect's Do
menu: File > New Scene...
prompt: Cards
create: Sprite
rename: Slime
set: Sprite.Tint = #57D36B
menu: Entity > Save as Prefab
menu: Entity > Delete
expectcount: Slime = 0
say: A slime, saved as a prefab.
create: Empty
rename: Slime Pit
set: Transform.Position = 6, 3, 0
add: Spawner
pick: Spawner.Prefab = Slime
set: Spawner.Running = false
explain: field:Spawner.Running | Only when told | A platformer's spawner, switched off, so it spawns a slime only when something tells it to.
deselect
create: Deck
select: Hand
set: Hand.StartWith = 0
create: Card
rename: Summon
add: Card Effect
pick: CardEffect.DoOn = Slime Pit
pick: CardEffect.Do = Spawn
expectvalue: Summon.CardEffect.Do = Spawn
explain: field:CardEffect.Do | Do | A card effect can do any action in the scene. This card does the spawner's Spawn.
play
wait: 1
gamedrag: Summon > Play Zone
waitfor: Slime | 3
explain: game | A slime | Playing the card spawned a slime by the pit. A card could open a door or start a lift the same way.
stop

chapter: A hotspot opens any door | A Hotspot's Use Do
menu: File > New Scene...
prompt: Vault
create: Walker
deselect
create: Sprite
rename: Vault Door
set: Transform.Position = -6, 1, 0
set: Sprite.Size = 1.5, 3
set: Sprite.Tint = #8A5A33
add: Door
set: Door.Locked = true
explain: component:Door | A locked door | A platformer's door, locked. It could be anywhere in the game.
deselect
create: Hotspot
rename: Lever
set: Transform.Position = 3, 0.5, 0
set: Hotspot.UseLine = Something clanks open.
pick: Hotspot.UseTargets = Vault Door
pick: Hotspot.UseDo = Open
expectvalue: Lever.Hotspot.UseDo = Open
explain: field:Hotspot.UseDo | Use Do | Using the lever does the door's Open: an adventure's hotspot can do any action, on anything.
play
wait: 0.5
gameclick: Lever
wait: 3
expectvalue: Lever.Hotspot.TimesUsed = 1
expectvalue: Vault Door.Door.Locked = false
explain: game | Open | The walker walked over and pulled the lever, and the vault door is open for good.
stop

chapter: A note fires a weapon | A Trigger hearing Hit
menu: File > New Scene...
prompt: Beat
write: Tables/Taps.table | mashup-ready-genres/Taps.table
create: Note Lanes
pick: NoteLanes.Chart = Taps
say: Note lanes, with a chart of notes on every half beat in the first lane.
deselect
create: Sprite
rename: Hero
set: Transform.Position = -7, 2, 0
add: First Person Movement
set: Body.GravityScale = 0
set: FirstPersonMovement.Controllable = false
explain: field:FirstPersonMovement.Controllable | The lanes have the input | The hero doesn't have the input: the lanes do, so D presses a lane rather than moving the hero.
add: Weapon
add: Trigger
pick: Trigger.Message = Hit
pick: Trigger.From = Note Lanes
pick: Trigger.Do = Fire
expectvalue: Hero.Trigger.Do = Fire
explain: field:Trigger.Do | Fire | When a note is hit, the hero's weapon fires. Its Fire action works whether or not the hero has the input.
deselect
create: Sprite
rename: Dummy
set: Transform.Position = 7, 2, 0
set: Sprite.Tint = #C04040
add: Box Collider
add: Health
set: Health.Max = 3
play
wait: 2.5
tap: D
wait: 0.6
tap: D
wait: 0.6
tap: D
wait: 0.6
tap: D
waitgone: Dummy | 3
explain: game | Three hits, three shots | Each note hit on the beat fired the weapon, and three shots finished the dummy.
stop

chapter: A bumper hurts a boss | A Trigger hearing a bumper
menu: File > New Scene...
prompt: Pinball
create: Pinball Table
deselect
create: Sprite
rename: Boss
set: Transform.Position = 13, 4, 0
set: Sprite.Size = 3, 3
set: Sprite.Tint = #C04040
add: Health
set: Health.Max = 3
add: Trigger
pick: Trigger.Message = Score
pick: Trigger.From = Bumper
pick: Trigger.Do = Damage
explain: component:Trigger | When a bumper scores | When a bumper sends its score, the boss takes a point of damage. A pinball table can fight a boss.
select: Ball
set: Transform.Position = -2.4, 5.5, 0
say: For the demo, the ball starts just over a bumper.
play
wait: 1
waitgone: Boss | 6
explain: game | Down | Three knocks off the bumper, and the boss is gone.
stop
say: Every genre names its actions and outputs, and what reads the input waits for focus. Griff's tests hold each genre to it, so the next one can't skip it.
